# Source documents (CCSS PDFs, NGSS standards, and — once permission exists —
# any College Board material) are fetched on demand by
# scripts/fetch_us_sources.py and never committed. Same policy as
# ../CAPS/past_papers/ and ../IEB/.
#
# sources_manifest.json (URL + sha256 provenance) IS committed; the curated
# .md and .json extractions carry everything consumers need.
#
# Note that audit_tree.py fails the build if a *.pdf is committed anyway, and
# separately fails if a sources_manifest.json appears under a framework whose
# rights gate is still closed.
*.pdf
source/
__pycache__/
